CommitDate: Tue Oct 13 04:29:02 2026 -0500

    fix(aug-096): warm per-namespace DuckDB connections at daemon startup
    
    The first namespace-scoped semantic request in a fresh daemon process paid
    connection creation (per-process scratch file) plus DuckDB's first
    read_json scan over the namespace's partition JSONL files, while the
    default namespace (already touched by startup traffic) answered in
    milliseconds. Every recall-bearing surface (recall, check, /api/recall,
    POST /check, serve search) paid that cliff once per namespace per restart.
    
    Fix: startNamespaceWarmup() runs fire-and-forget AFTER the TCP bind in
    startHttpMode — listen() is never delayed. It enumerates every on-disk
    namespace via the SAME census GET /api/namespaces unions
    (censusOnDiskNamespaces over resolveNamespacesPath(), which is also where
    request-time resolveNamespacePath sends ?namespace=<name>), then per
    namespace creates the singleton connection
    (getDuckDBConnection("singleton", namespacePath)) and, when the manifest
    lists partitions holding JSONL chunks, runs one trivial queryMemories page
    (limit 1) to force the first partition scan.
    
    Contract:
    - non-blocking: never awaited by the caller, never delays listen()
    - failure-tolerant: a namespace that fails to warm logs a warning, is
      evicted (so the first real request starts from a clean connection), and
      is skipped; the daemon never crashes or refuses traffic over warm-up
    - DUCKBRAIN_WARM_NAMESPACES=0|false disables the pass (default on)
    - one startup log line lists per-namespace warm-up ms, e.g.:
      [duckbrain] Namespace warm-up: 2 namespace(s) warmed, 0 skipped, 452ms
      total [big=452ms scanned, default=0ms connection-only]
    
    Tests (src/http/namespace-warmup-aug096.test.ts, 8 tests): warm-up creates
    singleton connections for every census namespace without any request and
    scans manifest-backed partitions; a failing namespace does not throw,
    other namespaces still warm, the failed one is evicted and warned; env
    guard off = zero warm-up work; corrupted manifest degrades to
    connection-only; unreadable namespaces root yields [] without throwing.
    
    Measured live (built daemon, 177MB/145k-row namespace, page cache evicted
    before start, list path with no q= so no embedding provider in the way):
    - warm-up OFF: first request 523ms, second 280ms
    - warm-up ON: warm-up pass 452ms at boot, first request 395ms, second 279ms
    The provider-bound share (query embedding + on-the-fly candidate embeds)
    is unaffected by design — that cost is identical scoped vs unscoped.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
    
    Guard note: the pinned pre-commit hook build (gitreins-DF-GITREINS-POC-88)
    cannot map TypeScript tests (its discovery only pairs tests/test_<module>.py),
